                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} category of coalgebras
                for any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} lex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
                on a topos is again a topos: a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+of+algebras+over+a+monad"} topos of coalgebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible
              %p
                For instance, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+gluing"} Artin gluing
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Gl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gl(F)
                is equivalent to the category of coalgebras for the comonad on the topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ×
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\times D
                defined by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↦
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ×
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,d) \mapsto (c, d\times F(c))
            %li
              %p
                More generally, the category of coalgebras for any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} pullback-preserving
                comonad on a topos is again a topos. This covers both the preceding result and also the overcategory (slice category) result above, since
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E/X
                is the category of coalgebras for the pullback-preserving comonad given by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi E
                        %mo →
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times - \colon E \to E
            %li
              %p
                More generally still,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"} Todd Trimble
                has a notion called a “modal operator” on a topos, from which one can construct a new topos of “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                \-structures”: see
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/toddtrimble/published/Three+topos+theorems+in+one"} Three topos theorems in one
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
                is a topos. A related idea is Toby Kenney’s notion of lex distributive
                = succeed "," do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    diad
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/diad"} ?
            %li
              %p
                From any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+combinatory+algebra"} partial combinatory algebra
                one can construct a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+topos"} realizability topos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
                is “computable” or “effective” mathematics relative to that PCA. In particular, for
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleene%27s+first+algebra"} Kleene's first algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+topos"} effective topos
            %li
              %p
                A topos can also be constructed from any
                = succeed "." do
